  "scope": "Three parsed constructor payload fixture pairs put a nested two-field constructor inside a tuple or either sum branch, followed by a scalar outer field. Each row requires recovery to reduce the inner constructor fields, the collection and the remaining outer field. Recovery compares the reduced annotation index with the reduced Pick index, so these rows do not detect field order. The constructor payload syntax row independently checks collection addresses, field order and outer resumption. Semantic variants change the Pick index spelling and recheck Pick and keep in the kernel. They check preparation and inline proof sealing and compare runtime output with opaque twins. The gate binds all three rows to their exact sources and variant modes. Six mutations drop semantic variants or bypass constructor field recovery. The three pass-through mutations apply the same edit and require different fixture failures. The constructor recovery control fails all three rows. The field order control fails only the syntax row. Every mutation requires a successful isolated build and its named failure.",
